{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJmxifJMkY9KMXxiyKDW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `ccode(sinc(x))` now prints `((x != 0) ? (\\n   sin(x)/x\\n)\\n: (\\n   1\\n))`. The existing C-printer and codegen tests all pass (83 passed).\n\nI made two additions to `sympy/printing/ccode.py`:\n\n- **`_print_sinc`**: rewrites `sinc(x)` as `Piecewise((sin(x)/x, Ne(x, 0)), (1, True))` and prints that, as the issue suggests.\n- **`_print_Relational`**: the C printer was outputting relationals in SymPy form, so the condition came out as `Ne(x, 0)`, which isn't valid C. This affected the issue's own `Piecewise` example too. Relationals now print with C operators: `Ne(x, 0)` gives `x != 0`, and `x < 1` gives `x < 1`.\n\nThe second change applies to all relationals, not just the ones inside `sinc`. So any existing `ccode` output that contains `Eq`, `Ne`, `<` and so on will now look different."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":20264,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1477},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9100044-e989-49e7-bd9b-e4f45edee54a","uuid":"6d25f9af-f9fc-4f6e-8484-de024a800c01","timestamp":"2026-11-22T22:44:08.039Z","request_id":"req_011ChJmxiX7cdFE8Rz1Fvvcz"}
